  "notes": "Revision after the failed check (KeyError on `location.latitude`): the coordinate fields are now `location#point`; nothing else changed. Replay of the contract's chain on raw_cache.parquet with a per-row point read of `location` (GeoJSON coordinates -> (lat=coords[1], lon=coords[0]); else float latitude/longitude), year from timecreate kept to 2018-2024, offense by the case-sensitive type_ map in offense_mapping.csv, disposition exclusion {VOI,UNF,DUP,TST,CBC}, drop null and (0,0) coordinates, de-dup on nopd_item: 197,689 rows kept. Per-cell comparison (pandas groupby year x offense on the replay) against the 40 oracle cells listed in the check result: 39 match exactly (e.g. 2018 aggravated_assault 1,908; 2021 larceny 15,020; 2024 burglary 2,009); 2023 motor_vehicle_theft is 8,952 vs oracle 8,951. The two cells not listed (2024 murder, 2024 robbery) replay to 110 and 722. The oracle total is 197,688; the 1-row difference is nopd_item H0995923 (2023, motor_vehicle_theft), the offshore point at [-90.47422562, 28.49213913] that falls in no Louisiana block group (README.md:130-131) and is dropped by the block-group join; well inside the 1% per-cell tolerance (1 of 8,951 in 2023 motor_vehicle_theft). Earlier findings stand: 222,381 raw rows; 0 unmapped type_; 18,470 dropped by disposition (README.md:78); 6,222 dropped for missing or (0,0) coordinates; 0 by year; 0 by de-dup; the rape rule yields 0 rows because every rape-coded row lacks coordinates (README.md:147); the 12 rows with disposition literal \"None\" are kept as in the script. Jurisdiction: NOPD feed (README.md:5-8), so New Orleans city only (197,585 incidents in evidence/jurisdictions.csv); the 108 others (nonmunicipal remainder 65, Gretna 37, Westwego 3, Kenner 2, Slidell 1) are edge spillover. source_kind is cad_dispatch: the feed is Calls for Service (01_fetch_nola.py:3-20; README.md:41-50).",
  "source_kind": "cad_dispatch",
